    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (77.62) and **Christian Yelich** (74.32) anchoring the offense, representing our most potent scoring threats against favorable matchups. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from an elite 0.448 xwOBA against Cecconi, while **Christian Yelich** is in a prime position to exploit Elder\u2019s slow delivery, maximizing his stolen base potential\u2014a crucial factor given our emphasis on the scarcity of the category. **Trea Turner** (68.44) and **Kyle Schwarber** (67.41) also present strong plays; while they face the tougher arm of Peterson, their batting order positioning and favorable platoon splits provide high-floor production that warrants inclusion.\n\nOutside of the core, **Lars Nootbaar** (64.36) is a high-upside start today, aided by beneficial wind conditions and a strong platoon edge against Kolek. Conversely, **Carson Benge** (45.89) is our most volatile start; while we expect him to lead off, he faces the formidable Wheeler, whose skill level significantly suppresses his overall efficiency score. Our most difficult decision on the bench involved **Caleb Durbin** (41.22). Although he profiles well for our speed-oriented strategy, he was edged out by higher efficiency scores from the active starters. Meanwhile, owners should note that **Pete Crow-Armstrong** has been removed from consideration due to a confirmed rainout. Aside from the weather risk in that postponement, our primary concern remains the tough assignment **Carson Benge** faces against Wheeler; if the confirmed lineup pushes him down the order, he remains a candidate for mid-game substitution to protect our league-wide daily game caps.",
